# Jarvis authority overlay

Cursor is the execution plane. Jarvis / Builder Core remains the authority plane.

Repo-native Cursor skills under `.cursor/skills/` (Team Kit, Superpowers, Cursor SDK guidance, CLI-for-Agents) are a **workflow library**. Use them when relevant. They do not replace the harness.

## Hard boundary

No imported Cursor skill, rule, subagent, SDK helper, CLI helper, or plugin workflow may independently declare or bypass:

- durable task identity
- factory run identity / fencing
- locked product intent
- locked acceptance / scorer authority
- path / resource ownership
- deterministic verification
- PASS / DONE authority
- exact-SHA evidence
- CI requirements
- retry limits
- production-credential restrictions
- GitHub merge authority

Workers never self-certify completion. Production / business credentials never belong in coding workers.

## Convenience skills that may HELP but cannot AUTHORIZE

These Team Kit skills may perform work (diagnose, patch, branch, open/update a PR, watch CI). They may **not** set Jarvis task PASS/DONE, merge eligibility, accepted evidence, task completion, or new product scope:

- `review-and-ship`
- `new-branch-and-pr`
- `loop-on-ci`
- `fix-ci`
- `fix-merge-conflicts`
- `make-pr-easy-to-review`

These Superpowers skills may guide process (brainstorm, plan, TDD, debug, review). They may **not** set Jarvis task PASS/DONE, merge eligibility, accepted evidence, task completion, or new product scope:

- `using-superpowers`
- `brainstorming`
- `writing-plans`
- `executing-plans`
- `subagent-driven-development`
- `test-driven-development`
- `systematic-debugging`
- `verification-before-completion`
- `finishing-a-development-branch`
- `requesting-code-review`
- `receiving-code-review`
- `multitask` (and `dispatching-parallel-agents`)
- Parallel web skills (`parallel-setup`, `parallel-web-search`, `parallel-web-extract`, `parallel-deep-research`, `parallel-data-enrichment`, `parallel-findall`, `parallel-monitor`)

`verify-this` and `verification-before-completion` produce local evidence only. That is not Jarvis PASS/DONE.

AGENTS.md and `docs/master-sot/` take precedence over Superpowers skill order (including "invoke before any response").

The `ci-watcher` subagent reports CI status. It does not authorize merge or task completion.

## Programmatic Cursor integration

`@cursor/sdk` via existing `CursorProvider` is the primary Jarvis programmatic Cursor integration. The Cursor Agent CLI binary (`agent`) is optional and not required.

See `docs/CURSOR_BUILDER_CAPABILITIES.md`.
